      "message": "Will \"temperature \u003e\u003d 45\" the only temp zones that need to handle specifically?\nRe: Yes. Cell charge operating temperature range is 0 ~ 60 C, and C-FET will be OFF when cell temperature is out of this range. EC will set request voltage and current base on smart battery desired voltage and current automatically when cell temperature is 0 ~ 60 C. But battery charged to 4.1V at 45℃ , the desired voltage of the smart battery is still 4.4V, this is only temp zones need to be handled specifically.\n\nWhat do you mean by finish this code base on these parameters?\nI wanted to do as below, please ignore it. Thanks!\nif (curr-\u003estate \u003d\u003d ST_CHARGE \u0026\u0026 bat_temp_c \u003e\u003d batt_info-\u003estart_charging_max_c * 10)\n     curr-\u003erequested_voltage\t\u003d 4100;",
